# Command rules. Format: decision|pattern tokens|justification
# Note: some entries duplicate the built-in approval screens (git reset --hard, git push --force, rm -rf, git diff, the AGENTS.md/MEMORY.md fences) and are kept as documentation.
# decisions: forbid > prompt > allow. In the interactive approval policy a
# "prompt" decision forces an explicit yes/no before the command runs; the
# token rules are matched per command segment at any token position with
# quotes stripped, and "allow" only relaxes an ordinary mutating verdict
# (it can never approve something the destructive screen caught).
# Regex rules: forbidre|<regex>|<justification> match the whole command text, so they catch
# shapes that span segments or wrappers. Regex matching is case-insensitive.
forbid|rm -rf|Destructive deletion; use careful targeted removal
forbid|Remove-Item -Recurse -Force|Destructive deletion; confirm scope first
forbid|git push --force|Force-push without lease can destroy history; use --force-with-lease
forbid|git reset --hard|Destructive reset; uncommitted work will be lost
forbidre|git\s+reset\s+--hard|Destructive reset, any position or wrapper
prompt|git push|Pushing to a remote changes shared state; logged
allow|git diff|Safe read-only diff
allow|git status|Safe read-only status
allow|git log|Safe read-only log
# Cache-prefix guards: AGENTS.md and the per-project MEMORY.md are loaded
# into the provider prompt prefix, and rewriting either mid-session
# invalidates the prompt prefix cache for subsequent turns (and the cost of a full re-bill).
# Shell-layer writes are forbidden; deliberate updates go through the
# instruction-audit / update-memory flows at session boundaries.
forbidre|(>|>>)\s*[^|\r\n]*AGENTS\.md|(set-content|add-content|out-file|new-item|remove-item|move-item|rename-item)\b[^|\r\n]*AGENTS\.md|Mid-session AGENTS.md edits invalidate the provider prefix cache; defer to session boundaries
forbidre|(>|>>)\s*[^|\r\n]*MEMORY\.md|(set-content|add-content|out-file|new-item|remove-item|move-item|rename-item)\b[^|\r\n]*MEMORY\.md|Mid-session native-memory fence edits invalidate the provider prefix cache; memory-mirror handles this at close

